 "notes": {
  "commentaries": "Three commentaries are used. The anonymous bhāṣya printed with the 80-anuvāka text in the Ānandāśrama pariśiṣṭa comments on this text in this order; its author is unknown and it largely follows Sāyaṇa, so it is cited as anonymous. Sāyaṇa (Vedārthaprakāśa) and Bhaṭṭa Bhāskara (Jñānayajña) comment on 64-anuvāka recensions — Sāyaṇa on the one vishvAsa calls Āndhra, Bhāskara on the Drāviḍa — whose order differs (the five ‘brahma’ mantras sadyojātam … are Sāyaṇa’s 43–47) and which lack the block of homa and japa mantras of anuvākas 51–64 here; they are reached through a computed concordance. A commentary of Raṅgarāmānuja on this Upaniṣad exists but is not in the edition’s sources, and is not cited. The sources are OCR-derived texts of printed books; print matter is removed on import.",
  "corrections": "No reading of the base has been changed. Where the two other witnesses agree against the base, the place is classed ‘verification required’ until it is checked against the printed sources.",
  "rights": "No modern translation was copied. The padaccheda, word tables, translations, explanations, commentary prose and studies are original to this edition, prepared for PaddySpeaks."
